{ "Identifier":       { "ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "UAD-MAD-V1.0-I01", "AIMName": "UAD-MAD-V1.0" },

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "User Agent for Multimodal Anonymous Dialogue: the application that interacts with the real world and with the MMC-MAD middleware via the north HCI API. It owns the real-world edge Modules - Speech Object Acquisition (mic - the human's spoken turn), Speech Object Delivery (the Machine Speech to the loudspeaker) and 3D Model Object Delivery (the avatar to the screen). It is trusted in its interaction with the middleware (across the HCI API) and untrusted in its interaction with the real world, which is why the acquisition and delivery edges are the User Agent's, not the middleware's. It supplies the human's turn to MMC-MAD (RecogniseSpeech / SubmitDialogueIntent) and presents the Speaking Avatar it receives (ReceiveSpeakingAvatar).",

